[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Knowledge and Progress]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.44]Lesson 22 | 第22课
[00:02.10]Knowledge and progress | 知识和进步
[00:08.93]In what two areas have people made no 'progress' at all? | 在哪两个方面人类根本没有取得“进步”？
[00:15.87]Why does the idea of progress loom so large in the modern world? | 为什么进步这个观念在现代世界显得如此重要？
[00:21.41]Surely because progress of a particular kind is actually taking place around us | 肯定是因为某种特定的进步确实正在我们周围发生，
[00:27.63]and is becoming more and more manifest. | 而且正变得越来越明显。
[00:30.31]Although mankind has undergone no general improvement in intelligence or morality, | 虽然人类在智力或道德方面没有得到普遍的提高，
[00:36.16]it has made extraordinary progress in the accumulation of knowledge. | 但人类在知识的积累方面取得了非凡的进步。
[00:41.37]Knowledge began to increase as soon as the thoughts of one individual | 知识一俟一个人的思想
[00:45.69]could be communicated to another by means of speech. | 能够通过语言传给另一个人，就开始增长了。
[00:50.02]With the invention of writing, a great advance was made, | 随着书写的发明，又前进了一大步，
[00:53.67]for knowledge could then be not only communicated but also stored. | 因为这样一来，知识不仅能够交流，而且能够储存了。
[00:58.66]Libraries made education possible, and education in its turn added to libraries: | 图书馆使教育成为可能，而教育反过来又增加了图书馆的藏书：
[01:05.39]the growth of knowledge followed a kind of compound interest law, | 知识的增长遵循一种复利法则，
[01:10.23]which was greatly enhanced by the invention of printing. | 印刷术的发明又大大加速了这一进程。
[01:14.03]All this was comparatively slow until, with the coming of science, | 所有这一切都相当缓慢，而随着科学的到来，
[01:19.53]the tempo was suddenly raised. | 节奏的速度突然加快了。
[01:21.95]Then knowledge began to be accumulated according to a systematic plan. | 于是知识开始按照一种系统的计划积累起来。
[01:27.44]The trickle became a stream: the stream has now become a torrent. | 涓涓细流汇成小溪，小溪现已变成了滔滔洪流。
[01:32.98]Moreover, as soon as new knowledge is acquired, it is now turned to practical account. | 此外，一旦获得了新知识，现在马上就会把它投入实际应用。
[01:39.18]What is called 'modern civilization' | 所谓“现代文明”
[01:42.01]is not the result of a balanced development of all man's nature, | 并不是全人类的天性均衡发展的结果，
[01:46.39]but of accumulated knowledge applied to practical life. | 而是积累起来的知识运用于实际生活的结果。
[01:51.47]The problem now facing humanity is: | 现在人类面临的问题是：
[01:54.53]What is going to be done with all this knowledge? | 所有这些知识将用来做什么？
[01:58.12]As is so often pointed out, knowledge is a two-edged weapon | 正如人们常常指出的，知识是一柄双刃剑，
[02:02.97]which can be used equally for good or evil. | 可以同样用于造福或作恶。
[02:06.88]It is now being used indifferently for both. | 而现在它正被不加区别地用于两个方面。
[02:10.65]Could any spectacle, for instance, be more grimly whimsical | 譬如说，还有什么景象比这更荒诞可怖
[02:14.99]than that of gunners using science to shatter men's bodies | 炮手用科学粉碎人的躯体，
[02:19.84]while, close at hand, surgeons use it to restore them? | 而就在近旁，外科医生却用它来恢复人的躯体呢？
[02:24.72]We have to ask ourselves very seriously | 我们必须十分严肃地问一下自己：
[02:27.64]what will happen if this twofold use of knowledge, | 如果知识的这种双重应用——
[02:31.66]with its ever-increasing power, continues. | 威力不断增长的双重应用——继续下去，将会发生什么？
